From 48452dbe47220b7a819886f59ce0adfe40a36921 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:36:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(app): refuse a 3+2 down-pointing tool axis that can
 go under the table

Past a 90-degree head tilt the tool axis points down toward the machine
table. The move from the tool-change height along it to the clearance
plane can end under the table top. #2987 gave only a note there, so the
post did not stop. The new verdict Warning::FirstTraverseUnderTable names
the highest plane that keeps the move over the table and says "lower the
clearance plane", never "raise". It blocks the post. Tilted caches read
Stale once (salt first-traverse-table-3081).

Fixes #3081

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
