From e82ca1d2d995a5c328bb28f204e81ae90fed224f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:45:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(examples): restamp the tilted example caches for the
 #3081 law

The tilted operations of three shipped projects read Stale once under the
new salt. Regenerated by the current law, their warnings, notes and moves
are the same (max deviation 5e-7 mm, the file's rounding), so only the
stamps change. No .nc file changes. The pinning test now reads the
verdict text, because this rig's B 120 face also fails the Z stroke law,
which refuses the post first.

Refs #3081

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
